  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kedar Sao vs The State Of Bihar on 5 September, 2016 Author: Sharan Singh Bench: Sharan Singh In The High Court Of Judicature At Patna Criminal Miscellaneous No.36743 of 2016 Arising Out of PS.Case No. -69 Year- 2006 Thana -Government Official C Darbhanga ====================================================== 1. Kedar Sao Son of Sukhdeo Sao Resident of Village - Munshi Bazar Asansol, P.S. and District - Burdwan (West Bengal) .... .... Petitioner Versus 1. The State of Bihar. .... .... Opposite Pa = = = = ====================== Appearance : For the Petitioner/s : Mr. Jitendra Narain Sinha For the Opposite Party/s : Mr. Md. Fahimuddin ====================================================== Coram: Honourable Mr. Justice Chakradhari Sharan Singh Oral Order 2 05-09-2016",
    "facts": "Allegedly, from the shop of one Sitaram Choudhary, at Darbhanga, certain food item (chanachur) was seized, which was found to be misbranded. He is said to have disclosed the Food Inspector that supply of the said food item was made by the petitioner.",
    "arguments": "Learned Counsel for the petitioner has submitted that only on the basis of the statement of the co- accused, petitioner has been named in the First Information Report. He has also submitted that there is no allegation of adulteration made in the First Information Report.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned Counsel for the petitioner has submitted that only on the basis of the statement of the co- accused, petitioner has been named in the First Information Report. He has also submitted that there is no allegation of adulteration made in the First Information Report.",
